      "branches": [
        {
          "summary": "Article 6.1.12(1). The payment discharges first any expenses",
          "rule": "ExpensesDischargedFirst"
        },
        {
          "summary": "Article 6.1.12(3)(d). Failing that, payment is imputed to the obligation which has arisen first",
          "rule": "ImputationByEarliestOrigin"
        },
        {
          "summary": "Article 6.1.12(3)(a). In the absence of imputation, payment is imputed to an obligation which is due or which is the first to fall due",
          "rule": "ImputationByFirstDue"
        },
        {
          "summary": "Article 6.1.12(3)(b). Failing that, payment is imputed to the obligation for which the obligee has least security",
          "rule": "ImputationByLeastSecurity"
        },
        {
          "summary": "Article 6.1.12(3)(c). Failing that, payment is imputed to the obligation which is the most burdensome for the obligor",
          "rule": "ImputationByMostBurdensome"
        },
        {
          "summary": "Article 6.1.12(2). If the obligor makes no specification, the obligee may within a reasonable time declare the obligation to which it imputes the payment, provided that obligation is due and undisputed",
          "rule": "ImputationByObligeeDeclaration"
        },
        {
          "summary": "Article 6.1.12(1). An obligor owing several monetary obligations may specify at the time of payment the debt to which the payment is to be applied",
          "rule": "ImputationBySpecification"
        },
        {
          "summary": "Article 6.1.13. Article 6.1.12 applies with appropriate adaptations to the imputation of performance of non-monetary obligations",
          "rule": "ImputationOfNonMonetaryPerformance"
        },
        {
          "summary": "Article 6.1.12(1). The payment discharges then interest due and finally the principal",
          "rule": "InterestDischargedSecond"
        }
      ],
